bevy-horizon: fold a storage access's constant offset into the access (NAK_DEBUG=ofold)

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 606441c9, after 0001-0020. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

NVK addresses storage buffers as nir_address_format_64bit_global_32bit_offset, so an access's
address is its binding's 64-bit base plus the u2u64 of a 32-bit offset. nir_opt_offsets can't
look through the u2u64 (NAK's TODO after nak_nir_opt_uniform_address gives the reason: it can't
tell that the 32-bit add doesn't overflow), so each field read through an index costs a 32-bit
add and a 64-bit one. On Maxwell that is three dependent instructions per load in Skate 3's
world fragment shaders.

With NAK_DEBUG=ofold, a pass before nir_opt_offsets rewrites base + u2u64(x + c), for a
constant c from 1 to 0x3fffff, as (base + u2u64(x)) + c. nir_opt_offsets then moves c into the
access, and CSE shares base + u2u64(x) between the accesses. This assumes x + c doesn't wrap at
32 bits. naga's clamped indices (bevy-horizon's BH_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS=clamp, its default)
keep every offset inside its binding, so there it can't. Without them it can only if the
shader's own index arithmetic wraps, as a[i + 2u] does with i = 0xfffffffe.

CSE leaves the shared address in the first block that needs it, where it holds two registers
until the last access: on its own, the first pass took a build of Skate 3's opaque world
fragment shader with fewer defines than the game's from 48 registers to 56, and so from 40
warps to 36. A second pass, after the last CSE, clones base + u2u64(x) into each block that
uses it, unless that block is in a loop the original isn't in, so only x stays live, as before.

NAK's statistics on a PC, for SM53 with clamped indices and the game's defines, before and
after (instructions; registers and warps don't change in any of these):

  Skate 3's opaque world fragment shader      2141 -> 2104
  its alpha-blended world fragment shader     1924 -> 1889
  its two-sided cutout fragment shader        1220 -> 1198
  its water fragment shader                   2861 -> 2782
  Bevy's mesh vertex shader                    153 ->  133
  Bevy's skinned mesh vertex shader            239 ->  202
  the triangle cull's list kernel              353 ->  277
  the triangle cull's cull kernel             1428 -> 1401
  the triangle cull's keep_marked kernel       727 ->  712

Switch builds start with ofold on, as with 0019's flags, and NAK_DEBUG=-ofold turns it off.
Other builds start with it off. NAK's flags key NVK's shader cache, in bits 48-63 of
nvk_physical_device_compiler_flags until now, and ofold is the 17th, so they move to bits
32-63 (32-47 were unused) and the compiler ABI revision goes from 10 to 11. On a PC, with
patch 0016, the 18 NAK tests that meson runs pass.

